
======== PART 1 - THE BUG: two sessions book the LAST seat with a plain SELECT count + INSERT ========
start: BOOKED=19 WAITLISTED=0 capacity=20
session A: sees 19 booked of 20 -> free seat, inserts member 248
session B: sees 19 booked of 20 -> free seat, inserts member 272
after both commit: BOOKED=21 WAITLISTED=0 capacity=20   <-- 21 BOOKED in a class of 20 (overbooked!)

======== PART 2 - UNIQUE (class_session_id, member_id): the same member booked twice at once ========
session B is blocked waiting for A's uncommitted row... alive
session B result: UniqueViolation: one_booking_per_member_per_class
final: BOOKED=20 WAITLISTED=0 capacity=20 (one booking for that member)

======== PART 3 - FIX 1: book_class() locks the class row (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) ========
session B called book_class() and is waiting on the lock: yes
session B finished after the lock released: status=WAITLISTED (waited 1.0s)
final: BOOKED=20 WAITLISTED=1 capacity=20   <-- exactly 20 BOOKED, the late one is WAITLISTED

======== PART 4 - FIX 2: SERIALIZABLE isolation (one of the two is aborted and must retry) ========
A: COMMIT ok
B: SerializationFailure (SQLSTATE 40001) - retry needed
final: BOOKED=20 WAITLISTED=0 capacity=20

======== PART 5 - READ COMMITTED vs REPEATABLE READ (non-repeatable read) ========
READ COMMITTED: reader's first count=10, after another session committed a booking, second count=11  -> CHANGED
REPEATABLE READ: reader's first count=10, after another session committed a booking, second count=10  -> same snapshot

======== PART 6 - DEADLOCK: two sessions lock the same two bookings in opposite order ========
A locked booking 78923; B locked booking 78924
A: DeadlockDetected (SQLSTATE 40P01) - victim rolled back
B: got second lock
fix: always lock bookings in the same order (ORDER BY booking_id ... FOR UPDATE) and the deadlock cannot happen.

All six demos finished.
